  </section>

  <section id="f-model">
    <div class="lab"><h2>Model issues</h2><p>Found while mapping every part and contact. They don't change the checks above, but the drawings should fix them.</p></div>
    <div class="body">
      <ul class="cond">
        <li class="info">Duplicates: 4 right poles and their lock pins, the right hooks at both ends, and every axle (two 1,309 mm tubes 53 mm apart at each position).</li>
        <li>Left rear tread pin is Ø10.73 in a Ø10 hole: it can't be assembled.</li>
        <li>Split pins sit beyond the pin ends, so they don't retain the nuts.</li>
        <li>Pole and lock pin overlap between z 87.5 and 225; pins, poles and slots are drawn line-to-line with no clearance.</li>
        <li>Left upper rail slots are about 9 mm out of line with the poles (3.6 mm clash); lower rails 1.6–2.6 mm.</li>
        <li class="info">The second base axle (x 9,936) isn't in the load path; the top bracket's fixing to the landing isn't modelled.</li>
        <li class="info">Zero-thickness “none” planes are in the file; they were ignored in all checks.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="f-sizes">
    <div class="lab"><h2>Smallest sizes that pass</h2><p>Same loads, same formulas. Treads re-run in FE; the rest sized by hand from the frame forces.</p></div>
    <div class="body">
      <div class="tw"><table>
        <thead><tr><th>Part</th><th>Now</th><th>Smallest that passes</th><th>For</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Tread</th><td>Open J + L, grating, no deck</td><td class="strong">Closed box 280 × 50: 5 mm serrated deck, 3 mm bottom, 5 mm webs</td><td>4 kN, crowd, one person (FE {BOX['ULS 4 kN front patch']['vm'] / FD:.2f})</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Tread pins</th><td>Ø10</td><td class="strong">Ø20 6082-T6, or Ø16 steel 8.8</td><td>{pin_v['value'] / 1000:.1f} kN + {pin_m['value'] / 1000:.0f} kNmm</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Fold lock</th><td>Ø2 latch pins</td><td class="strong">Ø8 pins, or a positive fold lock</td><td>{latch['value'] / 1000:.1f} kN per pole</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Guide rails</th><td>net W {min(wnet(k) for k in S):.0f}–{max(wnet(k) for k in S):.0f} mm³</td><td class="strong">net W ≥ 2,900 mm³ at the pin holes, or a mid support plus a proper lock</td><td>ULS crowd</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Right lower rail hole</th><td>12.5 above the edge</td><td class="strong">≥ {edge_req(edge_s) + 5:.1f} above the free edge</td><td>top-tread link force</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Base axle</th><td>Ø25 × 2.5, hook 70 mm off the jack</td><td class="strong">Jacks straight under the hooks (then Ø25 × 2.5 is enough), or Ø35 × 3; top axle Ø30 × 3</td><td>{ENV['R_base'] / 1000:.1f} kN per side, as drawn<span class="note">base fixed: Ø45 × 5, or jacks under the hooks with Ø30 × 3</span></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Hooks</th><td>10 mm plate, ring ≈ 22</td><td class="strong">Base ring ≥ 25.5 mm; top passes as drawn</td><td>{ENV['R_base'] / 1000:.1f} / {ENV['R_top'] / 1000:.1f} kN<span class="note">base fixed: 57.5 / 40 mm and a keeper for {ENVH['uplift_top'] / 1000:.1f} kN uplift</span></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Footplates</th><td>100 × 100 × 5</td><td class="strong">150 × 150 (R73); 5 mm is strong enough as drawn</td><td>R73</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Poles</th><td>RHS 25 × 10 × 2</td><td class="strong">Solid 25 × 39 (3.0 kN/m) to 25 × 51 (all barrier loads), or RHS 25 × 60 × 3 / 25 × 85 × 3; slots widen or poles go outside the rails</td><td>R142, R143, R179</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Top rail height</th><td>≈ 1,010</td><td class="strong">1,100 above the pitch line (+90 mm)</td><td>R63</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Open riser</th><td>125</td><td class="strong">≤ 120</td><td>R7</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
      <p class="dim">Each change, with drawings, is in the <a href="{BRIEF}">change brief</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="f-use">
    <div class="lab"><h2>Conditions of use</h2></div>
    <div class="body">
      <ul class="cond">
        <li>Not rated for public event use. The treads fail the 4 kN point load at the nosing ({t_front['util']:.1f}×) and sag {d_crowd['value']:.0f} mm under a crowd.</li>
        <li>The side frames stand only with every Ø2 latch pin engaged in both rails. At the design crowd load those pins are {latch['util']:.1f}× overloaded.</li>
        <li>Nobody may lean on the barriers: the poles carry {barrier_carried:.2f} kN/m against 3.0 required.</li>
        <li>As drawn, the base is free to slide and the frame sags {SLS['R base slides']['defl_sls']:.1f} mm against {sls_lim:.1f}. Fixing the base stiffens it, but then each jack takes {ENVH['H_base'] / 1000:.1f} kN sideways and each top hook lifts {ENVH['uplift_top'] / 1000:.1f} kN. Do that only with a designed base fixing and a keeper on the top hooks.</li>
        <li class="info">The top brackets need an anchor to the landing or cabin for {ENV['R_top'] / 1000:.1f} kN per side (ULS), or {ENVH['R_top'] / 1000:.1f} kN if the base is fixed. It's outside this model.</li>
        <li class="info">Capacities are calculated, not type-tested. Padding on the top rail is a user note, not part of these checks.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <footer>
    <span>Basis: v2/final/final_results.json, from tread_fe2.py (MITC4 shell FE, exact equilibrium), tread_vlasov2.py (branched thin-walled check), side_frame.py (OpenSees 2D frame), rail_checks_final.py, component_checks_final.py and tread_fe_box.py. Loads from v2/spec/sheet_2026-09-23_events.txt.</span>
    <span>Model: 25.9.2026 final STEP LADDER-standard.ifc · Blender: v2/final/FINAL_standard.blend (viewport colours show each part's result). Earlier load test: <a href="{REPORT}">Step Ladder Load Verdict</a>.</span>
  </footer>
</main>
"""

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ Rev A (kept as issued) + correction notice
head = ASIS[:ASIS.index("</style>")]
asis_main = ASIS[ASIS.index('<main class="sheet">'):ASIS.index("</main>") + 7]
asis_main = asis_main.replace('<section id="', '<section id="a-')
CORR = f"""
  <div class="corr">
    <span class="eyebrow">Correction · 25 Sep 2026</span>
    <b>Rev A's tread values were wrong</b>
    <p>Rev A treated the tread as a 280 × 50 plank. Measured part by part, it is an open J + L extrusion with a 5 mm deck, and the treads fail. Values for the 22 Sep model, re-run as a shell FE with a thin-walled cross-check:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>4 kN at the nosing: {aud_front['value']:.0f} MPa, {aud_front['util']:.2f}× · <b>fail</b> (Rev A showed a 7.67 kN capacity, pass)</li>
      <li>Crowd sag at the nosing {aud_crowd['value']:.1f} mm against 4.86 · <b>fail</b>; one person {aud_person['value']:.1f} mm · pass; 4 kN sag {aud_4f['value']:.1f} mm against 12.2 · <b>fail</b></li>
      <li>Tread pins Ø10, bending {aud_pin['util']:.2f}× on the right (14 mm lever), {aud_pin_t['util']:.2f}× with the rail's twist · <b>fail</b></li>
      <li>Right rail hole 2.5 mm from the free edge, {aud_edge['limit']:.1f} mm needed · <b>fail</b></li>
      <li>Material: f₀ is 250 MPa for t ≤ 5 mm (EN 1999-1-1 Table 3.2b); Rev A had 260 and 250 the wrong way round</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Everything else below is as issued on 23 Sep. The current issue is <a href="#final">DS-FMS-FINAL, Rev B</a>.</p>
  </div>
"""
asis_main = asis_main.replace("</header>", "</header>\n" + CORR, 1)
asis_main = asis_main.replace("<p>Issued after the final design has been load-tested, in this same layout so the two sheets compare line by line.</p>",
                              "<p>Issued after the final design has been load-tested, in this same layout so the two sheets compare line by line.</p>\n        <p>Now issued: <a href=\"#final\">DS-FMS-FINAL, Rev B</a>.</p>")

EXTRA_CSS = """
/* issue tabs */
.issues { max-width:1180px; margin:0 auto 26px; display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(230px,1fr)); border:1px solid var(--rule); background:var(--surface); }
.issues button { all:unset; box-sizing:border-box; cursor:pointer; display:grid; gap:3px; padding:10px 14px 9px; border-right:1px solid var(--rule); border-bottom:3px solid transparent; color:var(--ink); }
.issues button:last-child { border-right:0; }
.issues button[aria-selected="true"] { background:var(--accentbg); border-bottom-color:var(--accent); }
.issues button:focus-visible { outline:2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset:-3px; }
.issues span { font:500 11px/1 var(--mono); letter-spacing:.08em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--ink2); }
.issues b { font:600 18px/1.2 var(--display); }
.issues i { font-style:normal; font-size:12.5px; color:var(--ink2); }
/* utilisation ladder */
.ladder { background:var(--surface); border:1px solid var(--rule); padding:12px 14px 8px; display:grid; gap:7px; }
.lrow, .laxis { display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(150px,270px) minmax(0,1fr) 52px; gap:4px 14px; align-items:center; }
.lname { display:grid; gap:1px; min-width:0; }
.lname b { font-weight:600; font-size:13.5px; }
.lname span { font-size:12px; color:var(--ink2); }
.ltrack { position:relative; height:12px; background:var(--soft); }
.ltrack i { position:absolute; left:0; top:0; bottom:0; }
.ltrack i.pass { background:var(--pass); }
.ltrack i.fail { background:var(--fail); }
.ltrack::after { content:""; position:absolute; left:48.7%; top:-4px; bottom:-4px; border-left:2px solid var(--ink); }
.lval { font:500 13px var(--mono); font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; text-align:right; }
.lval.ok { color:var(--pass); } .lval.bad { color:var(--fail); }
.laxis .ticks { position:relative; height:16px; font:500 11px/16px var(--mono); color:var(--ink2); }
.laxis .ticks span { position:absolute; top:0; transform:translateX(-50%); }
@media (max-width: 560px) {
  .lrow, .laxis { grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) 46px; }
  .lname { grid-column:1 / -1; }
  .laxis > div:first-child { display:none; }
}
/* smallest-size box and correction notice */
.figs em { font-style:normal; font-size:12.5px; color:var(--ink2); }
.fix { background:var(--passbg); border:1px solid var(--rule); border-left:3px solid var(--pass); padding:12px 14px; display:grid; gap:6px; font-size:13.5px; }
.fix b { font:600 18px/1.25 var(--display); }
.corr { background:var(--surface); border:1px solid var(--rule); border-left:3px solid var(--fail); padding:14px 16px; display:grid; gap:8px; }
.corr b { font:600 20px/1.2 var(--display); }
.corr ul { margin:0; padding-left:18px; display:grid; gap:3px; }
td.bad { color:var(--fail); }
h3 { font-size:19px; font-weight:600; }
"""
LADDER_ONE = f"{pos(1.0):.1f}%"
EXTRA_CSS = EXTRA_CSS.replace("left:48.7%", f"left:{LADDER_ONE}")

SCRIPT = """
<script>
(function () {
  var tabs = Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('.issues button'));
  function show(id, scroll) {
    document.querySelectorAll('.doc').forEach(function (d) { d.hidden = d.id !== id; });
    tabs.forEach(function (t) { t.setAttribute('aria-selected', String(t.dataset.doc === id)); });
    if (scroll) window.scrollTo(0, 0);
  }
  tabs.forEach(function (t) {
    t.addEventListener('click', function () { show(t.dataset.doc, false); try { history.replaceState(null, '', '#' + t.dataset.doc); } catch (e) {} });
  });
  document.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
    var a = e.target.closest && e.target.closest('a[href="#final"], a[href="#asis"]');
    if (!a) return;
    e.preventDefault(); var id = a.getAttribute('href').slice(1); show(id, true);
    try { history.replaceState(null, '', '#' + id); } catch (err) {}
  });
  if (location.hash === '#asis') show('asis', false);
})();
</script>
"""

page = (head + EXTRA_CSS + "</style>\n\n"
        + '<nav class="issues" role="tablist" aria-label="Datasheet issue">\n'
        + '  <button type="button" role="tab" data-doc="final" aria-selected="true"><span>Current issue</span><b>DS-FMS-FINAL · Rev B</b><i>25 Sep 2026 final model</i></button>\n'
        + '  <button type="button" role="tab" data-doc="asis" aria-selected="false"><span>Superseded</span><b>DS-FMS-ASIS · Rev A</b><i>22 Sep 2026 model, with corrections</i></button>\n'
        + '</nav>\n'
        + '<div class="doc" id="final">' + FINAL + '</div>\n'
        + '<div class="doc" id="asis" hidden>\n' + asis_main + '\n</div>\n' + SCRIPT)
out = os.path.join(HERE, "web", "index.html")
open(out, "w", encoding="utf8").write(page)
print(f"wrote {out}: {len(page):,} chars; ladder {n_fail} fail / {n_pass} pass; crowd carried {crowd_carried:.2f}; barrier {barrier_carried:.3f}; edge {edge_up:.2f}/{edge_us:.2f} (tread-only {edge_tread_only:.2f})")
